# Performance (UI)

Full engine rules are in `docs/PLAN.md` §20. In Flutter:

- Dart is control plane only — no frame buffers, no audio samples in Dart.
- Scope `BlocBuilder` / `BlocSelector` to the smallest subtree that must rebuild.
- Do not wrap the whole `AppShell` in a builder that ticks every second; isolate timers to the recording indicator widget.
- Prefer `const` constructors for static subtrees; avoid rebuilding hidden tabs (shell already builds only the visible section).
- Heavy work: `compute()` or native side; never block `build()`.

```dart
// BAD — entire page rebuilds on every readiness poll
BlocBuilder<ReadinessCubit, ReadinessState>(
  builder: (context, state) => Scaffold(body: HugeTree(state: state)),
)

// GOOD — builder only around the part that changes (see home_page PageScaffold child)
```

When adding recording UI, assume recording is active: minimize animations, avoid large image decode on the main isolate.